# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Minseok Moon et al. (2025). Unveiling Defect Motifs in Amorphous GeSe Using Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   ACS Applied Materials & Interfaces. doi:10.1021/acsami.5c12334  arXiv:2506.15934v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2506.15934v1 (sha256 78be3efdc43a9cf7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 472 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/moon2025unveiling.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: BPNN (SIMPLE-NN), MTP (MLIP package, levels 26 and
# 20) and SevenNet models (NequIP-type, and MACE-type with self-tensor
# products at varying correlation order, depth and cutoff) trained on one
# GeSe dataset (crystal, liquid, quench, amorphous, melt, unary and
# interface MD; VASP PBE); the large-cell error check of the selected
# SevenNet model. Cubicity, ring statistics, DOS/IPR, sensitivity and
# defect analyses are properties.

