###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MTP training with a 16 A cutoff is estimated at about 40 days on one Intel Xeon 6226R CPU (Sec. 3.1.3); no such model was trained.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Per-model training and test RMSEs are in SI Table S1, not in the text read; the main text gives only ranges over models (test energy 4.4-9.7 meV/atom, force 0.16-0.28 eV/A, SevenNet lowest) and a BPNN energy offset of about 20 meV/atom.
# - The sevennet run is taken as the c4i4 model of Sec. 3.1.3, since both are four-layer, 4 A SevenNet models with a 16 A receptive field; the paper does not say whether they are the same training. Six-layer variants (Fig. S7) are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/moon2025unveiling.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

